{
  "configuration_id": "config_028",
  "reason": "All five completed experiments use singleprofile, leaving the profile-setting dimension entirely unexplored. The best singleprofile result is config_009 (rna_only, scvi_n200, acc=0.520), and the best overall is config_039 (multimodal, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, weighted, acc=0.537). Before investing budget in complex multimodal-multiprofile configurations, I need to know whether multiprofile actually adds signal. config_028 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) is the cleanest possible test: it matches config_009 in modality and RNA encoder, changing only the profile setting (and the necessary aggregation). If multiprofile with a simple avgpool aggregation improves on 0.520, it justifies exploring multiprofile multimodal configs (e.g., config_045). If it does not, we learn that profile multiplicity is not a useful axis and can redirect budget toward fusion-type or image-encoder comparisons. This single experiment reduces the largest remaining uncertainty with minimal confounding variables."
}

